/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.
    A function puts its argument into a table it makes, then stores what it makes into that element. Cast inside a rabbit, on a series from outside.

    A name records where the NAME was made; the store is judged against where what it reaches
    was made, which can be further out. Judged once everything is checked, so a later statement
    that lowers it counts too (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O2). */

Bind void to fill, given (the series of series of number rows):
    Define table as a series of series of series of number.
    Insert rows into table.
    Insert (a series of number with (1, 2, 3)) into item 1 of table.
Done.
Define keeper as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Cast fill on (keeper).
Done.
State keeper.
